# Seasons & Sights

Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TS + Tailwind. Full project context: [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).

## Commands

- `npm run dev` · `npm run build` · `npm start` · `npx vitest run` · `npx tsc --noEmit`

## Architecture

- Client routes import `@/data/regions-slim` and `@/data/events-slim` only — never heavy `@/data/regions` (server-only). `/api/region-detail` is the sanctioned client path to the heavy data.
- Trips: `src/lib/saved-trips.ts` is the single source; `src/lib/active-trip.ts` holds the active-trip pointer.
- Trip → itinerary resolution lives only in `src/lib/trip-plan.ts`; client views call `src/lib/trip-plan-slim.ts`. Don't reimplement the flexible-start rule per view.
- Auth/Supabase is lazy-loaded and must degrade gracefully when env vars are absent; remote failures go through `sync-status.ts`, never a silent `console.warn`.
- No `dark:` utilities — dark mode is remapped centrally in `src/app/globals.css`. New color families need a remap added there in the same commit.

## QA guardrails

- Test state **transitions**, not static state — see [docs/QA-JOURNEYS.md](docs/QA-JOURNEYS.md).
- Per-entity `localStorage`/DB keys MUST include the trip or destination id.
- Every bug fix gets a regression test in `test/`.
- Verify against a production build (`npm run build`) and hard-refresh before shipping.
